  "id": "wf4-verify-ambiguous-action-at-verify-time",
  "description": "If the action_id the Approval Gate emitted resolves to more than one register row at verify time, the branch halts rather than choosing.",
  "why_it_exists": "On the real MAT-20260101-002 snapshot the Actions register held TWO generations of rows written 39 minutes apart, so six action_ids each resolved to two rows carrying different action_types, recipients and channels. Approval Gate re-queried by action_id and simply took the last match, meaning WF4 could draft, approve and send against a row nobody chose - for example sending a CONTACT_INSURER letter to a car park manager. The Integrity Guard refuses to choose between duplicate rows, and Verify Selected Row re-checks the chosen row immediately before any writer or Gmail node runs. The guard scoped only the approved action; this proves that if the gate emits an action_id that is ambiguous - because the register changed, or because a future edit reintroduced ambiguity - the second gate still refuses to pick a row by recency or position.",
